  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-public",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -200,
      "w": 640,
      "text": "Public & auth \u2014 drafted from the Figma Landing, Admin Login and [FINAL] Membership Application frames.\n\nAssumed: Poppins; light theme only; landing pill goes to /apply and a small link to /login; footer email is a placeholder until the org picks one; social icons are placeholders until URLs exist.",
      "page": "public"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-login",
      "x": 720,
      "y": -200,
      "w": 640,
      "text": "Login \u2014 the Figma 'Forgot password?' link is omitted: the app has no self-service reset (recovery links are admin-sent, ADR 0004). Open question for a later ADR.",
      "page": "public"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-apply",
      "x": 1440,
      "y": -200,
      "w": 640,
      "text": "Apply \u2014 four steps with Next and Back (Ethan, 2026-09-08). Fields follow the designer's [FINAL] frame: no address block. The current code is one long page and still collects street address, city, province and postal code \u2014 the step form and the dropped fields are both code changes to settle before PR 1. 'Region' is kept because approval needs it. The 'What being a START member promises' card is deferred until the CCDO supplies copy.",
      "page": "public"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-privacy",
      "x": 2160,
      "y": -200,
      "w": 640,
      "text": "Privacy notice \u2014 rewritten in plain words for a college reader, no version line, no lawyer note. The wording here replaces docs/privacy/PRIVACY_NOTICE.md in PR 1 once Ethan and the CCDO approve it.",
      "page": "public"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-admin",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -200,
      "w": 640,
      "text": "Admin \u2014 the Figma Dashboard frame supplies the shell (white sidebar, pill nav, gradient active pill, SIGN OUT at the bottom, page title bar). Every screen keeps the app's current nav links, labels, columns and actions; only the look changes.\n\nNav pills, filter chips, tabs and dialogs are clickable inside each board.",
      "page": "admin"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-officer",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -200,
      "w": 640,
      "text": "Officer & Regional Representative \u2014 read-only surfaces. Officers see the directory columns only (no contact data); the RR sees their own region's contacts through the audited view.",
      "page": "officer-rr"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-components",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -200,
      "w": 640,
      "text": "Shared \u2014 the brand sheet: exact logo colours, the gradient wordmark, buttons, inputs, badges and alerts every board is built from.",
      "page": "components"
    }
